  "response": "Based on the provided vulnerability description, I will assess the CVSS v3.1 base metric.\n\n**Metrics Assessment**\n\n* **Attack Vector (AV)**: N (Network)\nThe vulnerability is related to an app reading sensitive location information, which can be accessed over a network.\n* **Attack Complexity (AC)**: L (Low)\nThe attack complexity is considered low as the vulnerability requires minimal effort and expertise to exploit.\n* **Privileges Required (PR)**: N (None)\nNo privileges are required to exploit this vulnerability.\n* **User Interaction (UI)**: N (None)\nNo user interaction is required to exploit this vulnerability.\n* **Scope (S)**: U (Unchanged)\nThe scope of the attack remains unchanged, as it only affects the affected app and does not spread to other systems or networks.\n* **Confidentiality Impact (C)**: L (Low)\nThe confidentiality impact is considered low as the vulnerability allows an app to read sensitive location information, which may be considered a moderate confidentiality risk.\n* **Integrity Impact (I)**: N (None)\nThere is no integrity impact, as the vulnerability does not allow an attacker to modify or delete data.\n* **Availability Impact (A)**: N (None)\nThere is no availability impact, as the vulnerability does not affect the system's ability to function.\n\n**Vector String**\n\nThe vector string will be in the format \"CVSS:3.1/AV:_/AC:_/PR:_/UI:_/S:_/C:_/I:_/A:_\"\n\n* CVSS:3.1/\n* AV:N\n* AC:L\n* PR:N\n* UI:N\n* S:U\n* C:L\n* I:N\n* A:N\n\n**Base Score**\n\nBased on the assessed metrics, the base score will be calculated as follows:\n\n* Confidentiality Impact (C): L (Low) = 0.1\n* Integrity Impact (I): N (None) = 0.0\n* Availability Impact (A): N (None) = 0.0\n\nThe base score is the sum of the weighted confidentiality, integrity, and availability impacts:\n\nBase Score = 0.1 + 0.0 + 0.0 = 0.1\n\n**Output**\n\nHere is the output in JSON format:\n\n```\n{\n  \"attack_vector\": \"N\",\n  \"attack_complexity\": \"L\",\n  \"p